<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ganden Monastery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1409</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Ganden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ganden Monastery is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhist</a> monastery on a mountain about 40 kilometres east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsongkhapa">Tsongkhapa</a> in 1409. It was the first and mother monastery of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelug">Gelug</a> school, whose head, the Ganden Tripa, is its abbot. It was one of the three great Gelug monasteries of Lhasa, was largely destroyed after 1959, and has since been partly rebuilt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ganden-monastery.jpg" alt="Ganden Monastery" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ganden_monastery.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
